IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-eligibility`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-amount`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-application`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-payment`

-- Tests for Regulations ss 7 to 9.1. Expected values are worked out by hand from the text,
-- with the working beside each assertion. The Consumer Price Index figure below is an
-- illustrative input, not a published figure.

§ `Regulations s 7 -- tests`

-- The month after the month of approval, across a month end and a year end.
#ASSERT `the first month for which a beneficiary is entitled to an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 10 1
#ASSERT `the first month for which a beneficiary is entitled to an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 10 1
#ASSERT `the first month for which a beneficiary is entitled to an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 7 1
#ASSERT `the first month for which a beneficiary is entitled to an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 1

§ `Regulations s 8 -- tests`

-- An otherwise eligible person (born 10 May 1990, DTC-eligible, resident, a citizen, return
-- filed, no partner, no custody, no suspension) asking about a month, with the return
-- either filed or not.
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      filed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`a person asking about` month `whose return is` filed MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS month
        `date of birth`                               IS YearMonthDay 1990 5 10
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS filed
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS NOTHING

-- A single beneficiary: adjusted income 30,000, working income 5,000 (A = 1: 166.67 a month).
`a single beneficiary's household` MEANS `Income and household facts` WITH
    `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month that precedes the month` IS FALSE
    `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS FALSE
    `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS FALSE
    `adjusted income without the income of a person who was the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS 30000
    `adjusted income as if the current spouse or partner had been the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS 0
    `the beneficiary's own working income` IS `Working income` WITH
        `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS 5000
        `net farming income`        IS 0
        `net fishing income`        IS 0
        `net professional income`   IS 0
        `net commission income`     IS 0
        `other net business income` IS 0
    `the working income of the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS `Working income` WITH
        `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS 0
        `net farming income`        IS 0
        `net fishing income`        IS 0
        `net professional income`   IS 0
        `net commission income`     IS 0
        `other net business income` IS 0

`the figures` MEANS LIST `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2024, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS 100

-- 8(1): entitled for the first month and every later month in which the person is eligible;
-- not for an earlier month, and not for a month in which a criterion fails.
#ASSERT `the beneficiary is entitled to an allocation for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 15) `whose return is` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the beneficiary is entitled to an allocation for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 15) `whose return is` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the beneficiary is entitled to an allocation for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) `whose return is` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the beneficiary is entitled to an allocation for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) `whose return is` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the beneficiary is entitled to an allocation for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 15) `whose return is` FALSE)
-- The amount for a month: 166.67 when entitled; 0 when not; not covered when s 6 has no
-- indexing factor for the payment period (June 2025 belongs to the period that began on 1 July 2024).
#ASSERT `the allocation payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 15) `whose return is` TRUE) `a single beneficiary's household` `the figures` EQUALS JUST 166.67
#ASSERT `the allocation payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 15) `whose return is` FALSE) `a single beneficiary's household` `the figures` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `the allocation payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) `whose return is` TRUE) `a single beneficiary's household` `the figures` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `the allocation payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (`a person asking about` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15) `whose return is` TRUE) `a single beneficiary's household` `the figures` EQUALS NOTHING

-- 8(2): twenty dollars or less (fork F10: above zero). 20.00 and 19.99 and 0.01 engage
-- it; 20.01 does not; nothing payable (0) does not.
#ASSERT `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` 20
#ASSERT `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` 19.99
#ASSERT `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` 0.01
#ASSERT NOT `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` 20.01
#ASSERT NOT `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` 0
#ASSERT NOT `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` 166.67

-- 8(2): the lump sum is the basic amount times the months remaining, the first payable
-- month counted. A basic amount of 15.00 in the period 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026:
-- from July, 12 months = 180; from November, 8 months (Nov to Jun) = 120; from June, 1 month = 15.
#ASSERT `the lump sum for the payment period` 15 (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (`the payment period that includes the day` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1)) EQUALS 180
#ASSERT `the lump sum for the payment period` 15 (YearMonthDay 2025 11 1) (`the payment period that includes the day` (YearMonthDay 2025 11 20)) EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the lump sum for the payment period` 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (`the payment period that includes the day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) EQUALS 15
-- A first payable month before the period began is counted from the period's first day.
#ASSERT `the lump sum for the payment period` 15 (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (`the payment period that includes the day` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1)) EQUALS 180

§ `Regulations s 9 -- tests`

-- Approved 15 September 2025: the first month is October. First payment made 20 December
-- 2025: October, November, December = 3 months; three amounts of 166.67 sum to 500.01.
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (LIST 166.67, 166.67, 166.67) EQUALS JUST 500.01
-- Made in the first month: one month.
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 10 3) (LIST 166.67) EQUALS JUST 166.67
-- A list that is too short or too long for the months is not covered.
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (LIST 166.67, 166.67) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (LIST 166.67, 166.67, 166.67, 166.67) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Made in the month of approval or before it: no months in the period; not covered.
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 9 30) (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 8 30) (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Across a payment period change (June 2026 at one rate, July and August 2026 at an indexed
-- rate of 178.33): approved 15 May 2026, first payment 10 August 2026: June, July, August.
-- 166.67 + 178.33 + 178.33 = 523.33.
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 10) (LIST 166.67, 178.33, 178.33) EQUALS JUST 523.33
-- Months in which the beneficiary was not eligible contribute 0.
#ASSERT `the first payment of an allocation` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 12 20) (LIST 166.67, 0, 166.67) EQUALS JUST 333.34

§ `Regulations s 9.1 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the form in which the supplemental amount is paid` EQUALS `paid as a lump sum`

§ `ss 5 and 7 together -- the month a person first qualifies is not paid`

-- An application received on 15 September 2025 by a person eligible from June 2025 is deemed
-- approved on the earliest eligible day (s 5(1)), which is in June 2025; entitlement then begins
-- with the month after the month of approval (s 7), that is July 2025. The month in which the
-- person first qualified is not paid (finding 4 in NOTES.md; the day within June does not matter, fork F13).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first month entitled for an application received on 15 September 2025 by a person eligible from the day` d MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (JUST d)
    WHEN JUST approved THEN JUST (`the first month for which a beneficiary is entitled to an allocation` approved)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `the first month entitled for an application received on 15 September 2025 by a person eligible from the day` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT `the first month entitled for an application received on 15 September 2025 by a person eligible from the day` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
-- Eligible from the first day of July 2025: paid from August 2025.
#ASSERT `the first month entitled for an application received on 15 September 2025 by a person eligible from the day` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1)
